WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.550
If both micro:bits have the same list, a place number is enough.

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:08.700
So you send the place number, not the word itself.

3
00:00:09.502 --> 00:00:13.077
The receiver shows the word at that place in its own list.

4
00:00:15.876 --> 00:00:19.876
The code only works if both lists match, in the same order.
